 "issue_title": "`safe_float_conversion` raises `OverflowError` instead of returning `(False, default)`",
 "issue_body": "**File:** `src/validation.py:536-540`\n\n```python\nresult = float(value)          # float(10**400) raises OverflowError\n```\n\n**Repro (verified):** `safe_float_conversion(10**400)` \u2192 `OverflowError: int too large to convert to\nfloat`. A JSON integer literal reaches this path. The string branch (`:543-549`) only catches\n`ValueError`, so the same gap exists there. The function's contract is \"never raises\".\n\n**Fix:** `except (ValueError, OverflowError): return False, default`.\n",
 "issue_url": "https://github.com/pmaasz/openLens/issues/340",
 "pr": 391,
 "pr_title": "fix(validation): honour safe_float_conversion's never-raises contract",
 "pr_body": "Closes #340\n\n## Problem\n\n`safe_float_conversion`'s contract is that it **never raises** \u2014 every caller consumes the `(success, value)` tuple. But the int/float branch called `float(value)` unguarded, and `float()` on a large int raises rather than returning `inf`:\n\n```python\nsafe_float_conversion(10**400)   # OverflowError: int too large to convert to float\n```\n\nA JSON integer literal reaches this path. The string branch only caught `ValueError`, so the same gap existed there.\n\n## Fix\n\nBoth branches catch `(ValueError, OverflowError, TypeError)`. The NaN/inf rejection and the bool rejection are untouched, so valid values still convert and a custom `default` is still honoured.\n\n## Tests\n\nFive tests added to `tests/test_validation.py`, **four fail without the change**: the two huge-int cases and the two subtests inside a never-raises sweep over 15 inputs (`None`, containers, `object()`, `'1e999'`, infinities, NaN\u2026). Two further tests pin that valid values still convert and that boundary floats are still rejected \u2014 the guard must not over-reject.",
 "fix_commit": "de5009777995f4359aefeb68d57ee1f6073936c5",
